## Notes

- Substitution variables (`${env}`, `${baseDomain}`, ...) are set once per
  cluster in `clusters/<env>/infra/sync.yaml` and passed down to every
  service via `postBuild.substitute`.
{{- if has "weave-gitops" }}
- weave-gitops ships with a placeholder admin password hash. Generate a real
  one with `gitops get bcrypt-hash` and update
  `infra/services/weave-gitops/_base/helmrelease.yaml` (escape `$` as `$$`).
{{- end }}
{{- if has "secret-stores" }}
- The vault ClusterSecretStore expects a `vault-token-global` Secret in the
  external-secrets namespace after you initialize and unseal Vault.
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .C.Provider "gcp" }}
- cert-manager and external-dns assume Workload Identity bindings to GCP
  service accounts with DNS admin on project `{{ "${gcloudProjectId}" }}`.
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .C.Provider "aws" }}
- cert-manager and external-dns assume IRSA roles (`cert-manager`,
  `external-dns`) with Route53 access.
{{- end }}
- Tenants get a namespace-scoped reconciler ServiceAccount. For a hard
  multi-tenancy lockdown, also enable flux's multitenancy flags
  (`--no-cross-namespace-refs`, `--default-service-account`).
